%9Setting:%9

    print_whois_rpl_in_server_window (boolean; default: OFF, the Shellter
    default configuration sets ON)

%9Description:%9

    Prints WHOIS and WHOWAS replies in the network's status window.

    That is the window named after the server tag, so a WHOIS typed in a
    channel does not clutter the channel.

    The window for the replies is chosen in this order:

        1. this setting: the network's status window,
        2. print_whois_rpl_in_active_window: the active window,
        3. otherwise the usual window: a query with the nick, or the window
           that matches the message level.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET print_whois_rpl_in_server_window on
    /SET print_whois_rpl_in_server_window off

%9See also:%9

    SET, WHOIS, WHOWAS, PRINT_WHOIS_RPL_IN_ACTIVE_WINDOW
